Gadema_Api_Test_Suite_Story.http

# GaDeMa API Test Suite — Writing Domain
# Focus: Story Outline, Scenes, Characters, World-Building, Dialogue

> **Protocol:** `HTTP/1.1` | **Base URL:** `http://localhost:5000/api/v1`  
> **Format:** RFC 2616-compliant with VS Code REST Client extension syntax

---

🧪 VS Code REST Client Tips
To use these in VS Code:

Install the REST Client extension (Huachao Mao)
Save this file as docs/GaDeMa_Writing_Domain_Test_Suite.http
Run with: Ctrl+Alt+N or click "▶ Send Request" in the editor
Responses appear below each request automatically
Pro tips:

Replace all <*_ID_FROM_STEP_X> placeholders with actual IDs returned from previous requests
Use environment variables for repeated values: {{PROJECT_ID}}, {{TOKEN}}
Chain requests using response variables: @PROJECT_ID = response.body.data.id
The sequence follows a realistic writer's workflow: Project → Story → Outline → Beats → Chapters → Scenes → Characters → World → Dialogue
Deletion steps (46-56) reverse the creation order to test cascade behavior
This test suite covers the complete Writing domain workflow:

Narrative Structure: Story → StoryOutline → OutlineSections → StoryBeats → StoryChapters → Scenes
Character Management: Characters → CharacterStates → CharacterRelations
World-Building: Factions → WorldLocations (hierarchical)
Dialogue Trees: DialogueBranches → DialogueNodes (tree structure)
Full CRUD: Create, Read, Update, Delete for all entities
Relationships: Linking Beats to Sections, Scenes to Beats, Characters to Relations
Error Handling: 404, 401, 400 tests


## 📋 Prerequisites: Authentication & Project Setup

```http
### ===== STEP 1: REGISTER A NEW USER =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/email/register HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "Email": "writer@example.com",
    "Password": "SecureP@ssw0rd!",
    "PasswordConfirmation": "SecureP@ssw0rd!",
    "Name": "Jane Writer"
}
###

### ===== STEP 2: SIGN IN =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/auth/email/signin HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
    "email": "writer@example.com",
    "password": "SecureP@ssw0rd!"
}
###

### ===== STEP 3: CREATE A NEW PROJECT =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/projects HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "title": "Fantasy RPG: The Lost Kingdom",
    "description": "A narrative-driven RPG with branching dialogue and character relationships.",
    "visibility": 0,
    "slug": "lost-kingdom"
}
###

### ===== STEP 4: CREATE STORY =====
POST https://localhost:5001/api/v1/projects/<PROJECT_ID_FROM_STEP_3>/stories HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:5001
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_STEP_2>

{
    "createData": {
        "title": "The Lost Kingdom Saga",
        "slug": "lost-kingdom-saga",
        "shortDesc": "Main story arc spanning three acts.",
        "status": 0,
        "isPublic": false
    },
    "description": "The complete narrative arc of the Lost Kingdom, including character journeys and world events."
}
###

